TYPE UDT_ShredderSequencerIO
  ROOTID 0
  MEMBERS
    CycleStart : Bool
    AutoStartSignal : Bool COMMENT "In: C-115 handshake vocabulary (owner ruling 2026-07-17, task 09, resolution 2) - external run permission, caller-asserted, named after the site's real chained-permissive pattern (FB_MotorFwdRevSystem.IO.AutoStartSignal), not doc 06's illustrative name. Unwired by FC_ControlMain for now - CycleStart/CycleStop already carry this sequencer's actual start/stop triggering; C-115 requires the vocabulary member regardless of whether this integration uses it."
    CycleStop : Bool
    DownstreamRunning : Bool
    SystemHealthy : Bool COMMENT "In (FC_ControlMain, from DB_Input.Control_Healthy): safety/control circuit healthy. Loss asserts StopCmd - every step aborts to Idle and a fresh CycleStart press is required after recovery, so an E-stop reset can never self-restart the plant (REQ-062)."
    DischargeConvRunning : Bool
    HopperLevelHigh : Bool
    ShredderRunFwdFB : Bool
    ShredderRunRevFB : Bool COMMENT "In (FC_ControlMain, from DB_Input.Shredder_Run_Rev_FB): confirmed reverse-running feedback. Step 30's ReverseRunTimer times this, not bare step dwell, so ShredderReverseRunTime buys actual reverse rotation, not a motor-off pause (REQ-005)."
    ShredderMotorCurrent : Real
    MotorFaultActive : Bool
    FaultReset : Bool
    OperatorPusherMode : Int
    PusherJogPreStartSounder : Bool
    Step : Int
    DischargeConveyorTimeoutFault : Bool
    ShredderBlockedFault : Bool
    RunDischargeConv : Bool
    RunInfeedConv : Bool
    EnableUpstream : Bool COMMENT "Out: this sequencer's C-115 ready-equivalent (owner ruling 2026-07-17, task 09 resolution 2) - asserted once Step 50 (Running) has held long enough (UpstreamEnableTimer, NETWORK 11) that whatever's downstream may enable. Same role as FB_MotorFwdRevSystem.IO.UPSEnable under this project's own established name for this signal - not duplicated under the generic vocabulary name."
    PreStartSounder : Bool
    InCycle : Bool COMMENT "Out: this sequencer's C-115 running-equivalent (owner ruling 2026-07-17, task 09 resolution 2) - Step <> 0 (NETWORK 15), same shape as the pusher's own Cycling. Was previously an unwritten dead member (standing C-610 finding); wiring it to satisfy C-115's running slot closes that finding too."
    MotorReverseCmd : Bool
    MotorAutoStartCmd : Bool
    MotorPreStartDoneCmd : Bool
    MotorStartArm : Bool COMMENT "Out: asserted through PreStart (Step 10) only - one fresh, operator-commanded start attempt arms the motor once. FC_ControlMain ORs it into the imported motor FB's RecentStart, which that FB self-clears once running or faulted (its own press-to-arm contract), so no restart happens without a new cycle start (REQ-062)."
    PusherModeCmd : Int
    PusherParkCmd : Bool COMMENT "Out: pre-start park request to the pusher - held through the machine-start steps 20-40 (range intent per C-603: any step inserted inside the start ramp still wants the pusher home) so the pusher reparks-with-warning if off home once the siren phase completes (REQ-045)."
    PusherCycleInhibitCmd : Bool COMMENT "Out: mirrors StopCmd - while the plant has any live stop reason (stop button, downstream lost, circuit unhealthy) the pusher must not launch or continue a cycle into the stopped plant (owner amendment 2026-07-16). Unlike the mode-0 force, this leaves hand-jog available: jog is blocked only by the stop button or an unhealthy circuit, never by downstream absence (REQ-040)."
